1739	/// `GET /-/v1/search?text=...&size=...` — npm search v1 endpoint.
1740	///
1741	/// Local-only: scans the on-disk storage and matches package names
1742	/// as a case-insensitive substring on `text`. Matches verdaccio's
1743	/// default behavior. We deliberately do NOT proxy to upstream npm
1744	/// even in proxy mode — the tests rely on the local-search semantics
1745	/// (`releasing/commands/test/search.ts` asserts that a guaranteed-not
1746	/// -to-exist query returns "No packages found", which an upstream
1747	/// proxy can't deliver because npm's search is fuzzy and returns
1748	/// dozens of unrelated matches for almost anything).
1749	///
1750	/// Results are filtered by the per-package access policy: a package
1751	/// the caller can't read (e.g. anonymous + `@private/*` or
1752	/// `@pnpm.e2e/needs-auth` with the default rules) is dropped from
1753	/// `objects` before the response is built. Without this the search
1754	/// endpoint would happily enumerate protected packages that the
1755	/// packument and tarball GETs correctly hide behind 401.
